## 2. DOMAIN GENERATION ALGORITHM (DGA)

### **DGA Algorithm Specification**
**Seed:** Exercise date + fixed salt (`REDTEAM2024_EXERCISE`)
**TLD Pool:** `["training.local", "redteam.lab", "exercise.internal"]`
**Domain Length:** 8-16 characters
**Character Set:** `a-z0-9`

### **DGA Implementation (C)**
```c
// dga.c - Domain Generation Algorithm
#include <stdint.h>
#include <string.h>
#include <time.h>

static const char charset[] = "abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyz0123456789";
static const char* tlds[] = {"training.local", "redteam.lab", "exercise.internal"};
static const int tld_count = 3;

uint32_t dga_seed() {
    time_t now = time(NULL);
    uint32_t seed = (uint32_t)(now / 86400); // Daily seed
    seed ^= 0x5245445445414D; // "REDTEAM" XOR
    return seed;
}

void generate_domain(char* domain, int len) {
    uint32_t seed = dga_seed();
    uint32_t state = seed;

    for (int i = 0; i < len; i++) {
        state = state * 1103515245 + 12345; // Linear congruential generator
        domain[i] = charset[state % 62];
    }
    domain[len] = '\0';

    // Append TLD
    int tld_idx = (seed >> 16) % tld_count;
    strcat(domain, ".");
    strcat(domain, tlds[tld_idx]);
}

char* get_c2_domain() {
    static char domain[64];
    generate_domain(domain, 12); // 12-char domain + TLD
    return domain;
}
```

